//@version=6
//@description Shared divergence structure, line, label, live-preview, slot-budget, and pivot context box helpers for MYNAMEISBRANDON Pine scripts.

library("DivergenceLineLabelOutput_Utilities", true)

// ==============================================================================================
// 🟢 REGION: Library Overview
// ==============================================================================================
//
// DivergenceLineLabelOutput_Utilities is an engine-agnostic divergence output library.
//
// This library is designed to help MYNAMEISBRANDON scripts render confirmed divergence,
// structure context, live-preview lines, labels, and pivot context boxes in a consistent
// way across oscillator systems such as RSI, MACD Composite, VFI, pressure oscillators,
// stack-bias tools, and future oscillator scripts.
//
// Important design note:
//
// • This library does not confirm pivots.
// • This library does not calculate RSI, MACD, VFI, or any oscillator.
// • This library does not decide which pivots are valid.
// • This library does not decide which source should be used for price or oscillator anchors.
// • This library does not decide whether a box should be upper, lower, price-based, or oscillator-based.
// • The calling script remains responsible for the pivot engine, oscillator engine, input logic,
//   colors, visibility modes, and final divergence/context/box conditions.
//
// What this library provides:
//
// • HH / LH / HL / LL / EQ structure text helpers
// • Regular / hidden divergence state helpers
// • Same-structure context state helpers
// • Divergence and context color routing helpers
// • Standardized divergence/context label text helper
// • Line-style and label-size resolvers
// • Confirmed price-pane line helpers
// • Confirmed oscillator-pane line helpers
// • Confirmed price-pane label helpers
// • Confirmed oscillator-pane label helpers
// • Matching color-array storage for confirmed objects
// • Indexed Last-N line and label helpers
// • Indexed Last-N pruning helpers for lines and labels
// • Slot-budget visibility helpers for confirmed lines and labels
// • Last-N-aware native-pane and price-pane box wrappers
// • Live-preview price-pane line and label helpers
// • Live-preview oscillator-pane line and label helpers
// • Pivot context box bounds helper
// • Native-pane pivot context box manager
// • Price-pane pivot context box manager using force_overlay=true
//
// Divergence model:
//
// • Regular bearish divergence:
//   - Price makes HH while oscillator makes LH
//
// • Regular bullish divergence:
//   - Price makes LL while oscillator makes HL
//
// • Hidden bearish divergence:
//   - Price makes LH while oscillator makes HH
//
// • Hidden bullish divergence:
//   - Price makes HL while oscillator makes LL
//
// Structure context model:
//
// • High-side continuation:
//   - Price makes HH while oscillator also makes HH
//
// • High-side fading:
//   - Price makes LH while oscillator also makes LH
//
// • Low-side continuation:
//   - Price makes LL while oscillator also makes LL
//
// • Low-side lifting:
//   - Price makes HL while oscillator also makes HL
//
// Structure context notes:
//
// • Structure context pairs are not divergence signals.
// • Context pairs show same-structure agreement between price and oscillator.
// • Context outputs should usually use their own line/label arrays and their own max-line budget.
// • Live-preview helpers are mainly intended for regular and hidden divergence candidates.
// • Context lines are usually best handled as confirmed-pivot outputs only.
//
// Pivot context box model:
//
// • Pivot context boxes are optional visual zones around confirmed pivot anchors.
// • They can help frame the oscillator or price zones where divergence/context pivots formed.
// • Confirmed oscillator peaks can be used for upper native-pane boxes.
// • Confirmed oscillator dips can be used for lower native-pane boxes.
// • Confirmed price pivots can be used for price-pane boxes with force_overlay=true.
// • Box visibility, colors, transparency, border style, and box memory remain controlled by the calling script.
// • Pivot context boxes are visual context only; they are not divergence signals by themselves.
//
// Label text model:
//
// • Full:
//   - Shows type, side, price structure, and oscillator structure with $ / osc prefixes.
//
// • No Prefix:
//   - Shows type, side, and the structure pair on separate lines.
//
// • Type Only:
//   - Shows only the label type and side.
//
// Slot-budget model:
//
// • Max Regular Lines = total visible regular divergence budget
// • Max Hidden Lines = total visible hidden divergence budget
// • Max Context Lines = total visible structure context budget when the calling script supports it
// • A live regular divergence can consume one regular slot while active
// • A live hidden divergence can consume one hidden slot while active
// • Confirmed lines and labels are not deleted when live preview is active
// • Confirmed lines and labels can be temporarily hidden when live preview needs the slot
//
// Example:
//
// • Max Regular Lines = 1
//   - Live regular active = live regular only
//   - No live regular = latest confirmed regular only
//
// • Max Regular Lines = 2
//   - Live regular active = live regular + latest confirmed regular
//   - No live regular = latest two confirmed regular lines
//
// Pane behavior:
//
// • Price helpers use force_overlay=true.
//   - These draw on the main chart from overlay=false scripts.
//   - These also work normally from overlay=true scripts.
//
// • Oscillator/native helpers do not use force_overlay.
//   - These draw in the script's native pane.
//   - In overlay=false scripts, this is the oscillator pane.
//   - In overlay=true scripts, this is still the price pane.
//
// Recommended usage:
//
// • Use price helpers for price-pane divergence outputs.
// • Use oscillator helpers from overlay=false oscillator scripts.
// • Use separate arrays for regular, hidden, and context outputs.
// • Use pivot context boxes as optional visual support around confirmed pivot anchors.
// • For overlay=true scripts, usually expose Price Only / Hide output modes.
// • For overlay=false oscillator scripts, Price + Oscillator / Price Only / Oscillator Only / Hide
//   output modes work well.
//
// ==============================================================================================
// 🔴 END REGION: Library Overview
// ==============================================================================================


// ==============================================================================================
// 📚 LIBRARY MAP
// ==============================================================================================
//
// DivergenceLineLabelOutput_Utilities is organized into:
//
// • Structure + Divergence State Helpers
// • Style + Label Helpers
// • Confirmed Line Array Helpers
// • Confirmed Label Array Helpers
// • Indexed Last-N Object Helpers
// • Confirmed Slot Visibility Helpers
// • Live Preview Line Helpers
// • Live Preview Label Helpers
// • Pivot Context Box Helpers
//
// ==============================================================================================

// ==============================================================================================
// 🟢 REGION: Structure + Divergence State Helpers
// ==============================================================================================

// @function Resolves HH/LH/HL/LL/EQ structure text from current and previous pivot values.
// @param curr Current pivot value.
// @param prev Previous pivot value.
// @param isHigh True for high-side pivot comparison, false for low-side pivot comparison.
// @returns Structure string: HH, LH, HL, LL, or EQ.
export divStructure(float curr, float prev, bool isHigh) =>
    curr > prev ? (isHigh ? "HH" : "HL") :
     curr < prev ? (isHigh ? "LH" : "LL") : "EQ"

// @function Resolves regular/hidden divergence states from price and oscillator structure strings.
// @param priceStruct Price structure string.
// @param oscStruct Oscillator structure string.
// @returns regularBear, regularBull, hiddenBear, hiddenBull, anyDivergence.
export divState(string priceStruct, string oscStruct) =>
    bool regularBear = priceStruct == "HH" and oscStruct == "LH"
    bool regularBull = priceStruct == "LL" and oscStruct == "HL"
    bool hiddenBear = priceStruct == "LH" and oscStruct == "HH"
    bool hiddenBull = priceStruct == "HL" and oscStruct == "LL"
    bool anyDiv = regularBear or regularBull or hiddenBear or hiddenBull

    [regularBear, regularBull, hiddenBear, hiddenBull, anyDiv]

// @function Resolves same-structure / context states from price and oscillator structure strings.
// @param priceStruct Price structure string.
// @param oscStruct Oscillator structure string.
// @returns highContinuation, highFade, lowContinuation, lowLift, anyContext.
export divContextState(string priceStruct, string oscStruct) =>
    bool highContinuation = priceStruct == "HH" and oscStruct == "HH"
    bool highFade = priceStruct == "LH" and oscStruct == "LH"
    bool lowContinuation = priceStruct == "LL" and oscStruct == "LL"
    bool lowLift = priceStruct == "HL" and oscStruct == "HL"
    bool anyContext = highContinuation or highFade or lowContinuation or lowLift

    [highContinuation, highFade, lowContinuation, lowLift, anyContext]

// @function Resolves the matching divergence color from caller-supplied colors.
// @param priceStruct Price structure string.
// @param oscStruct Oscillator structure string.
// @param regularBearColor Regular bearish divergence color.
// @param regularBullColor Regular bullish divergence color.
// @param hiddenBearColor Hidden bearish divergence color.
// @param hiddenBullColor Hidden bullish divergence color.
// @param highContinuationColor Optional color for HH/HH continuation pairs.
// @param lowContinuationColor Optional color for LL/LL continuation pairs.
// @param highFadeColor Optional color for LH/LH same-side pairs.
// @param lowLiftColor Optional color for HL/HL same-side pairs.
// @param fallbackColor Fallback color.
// @returns Resolved color.
export divColor(
     string priceStruct,
     string oscStruct,
     color regularBearColor,
     color regularBullColor,
     color hiddenBearColor,
     color hiddenBullColor,
     color highContinuationColor,
     color lowContinuationColor,
     color highFadeColor,
     color lowLiftColor,
     color fallbackColor) =>

    priceStruct == "HH" and oscStruct == "LH" ? regularBearColor :
     priceStruct == "LL" and oscStruct == "HL" ? regularBullColor :
     priceStruct == "LH" and oscStruct == "HH" ? hiddenBearColor :
     priceStruct == "HL" and oscStruct == "LL" ? hiddenBullColor :
     priceStruct == "HH" and oscStruct == "HH" ? highContinuationColor :
     priceStruct == "LL" and oscStruct == "LL" ? lowContinuationColor :
     priceStruct == "LH" and oscStruct == "LH" ? highFadeColor :
     priceStruct == "HL" and oscStruct == "HL" ? lowLiftColor : fallbackColor

// ==============================================================================================
// 🔴 END REGION: Structure + Divergence State Helpers
// ==============================================================================================


// ==============================================================================================
// 🟢 REGION: Style + Label Helpers
// ==============================================================================================

// @function Resolves Pine line style from a user-facing string.
// @param styleIn Style string: Solid, Dashed, or Dotted.
// @returns Pine line style.
export divLineStyle(simple string styleIn) =>
    styleIn == "Solid" ? line.style_solid :
     styleIn == "Dashed" ? line.style_dashed : line.style_dotted

// @function Resolves Pine label size from a user-facing string.
// @param sizeIn Size string.
// @returns Pine label size.
export divLabelSize(simple string sizeIn) =>
    sizeIn == "Tiny" ? size.tiny :
     sizeIn == "Small" ? size.small :
     sizeIn == "Normal" ? size.normal :
     sizeIn == "Large" ? size.large :
     sizeIn == "Huge" ? size.huge : size.small

// @function Returns black or white text depending on background brightness.
// @param bg Background color.
// @returns Contrast text color.
export divContrastText(color bg) =>
    float r = color.r(bg)
    float g = color.g(bg)
    float b = color.b(bg)
    float lum = (r * 0.299) + (g * 0.587) + (b * 0.114)

    lum > 150 ? color.black : color.white

// @function Builds standardized divergence label text.
// @param divType Label type text, usually Reg or Hid.
// @param divSide Label side text, usually Bull or Bear.
// @param priceStruct Price structure string.
// @param oscStruct Oscillator structure string.
// @param formatMode Label format mode: Full, No Prefix, or Type Only.
// @returns Formatted divergence label text.
export divLabelText(
     simple string divType,
     simple string divSide,
     string priceStruct,
     string oscStruct,
     simple string formatMode) =>

    formatMode == "Type Only" ? divType + "\n" + divSide :
     formatMode == "No Prefix" ? divType + "\n" + divSide + "\n" + priceStruct + "\n" + oscStruct :
     divType + "\n" + divSide + "\n$ " + priceStruct + "\nosc " + oscStruct
     
// ==============================================================================================
// 🔴 END REGION: Style + Label Helpers
// ==============================================================================================


// ==============================================================================================
// 🟢 REGION: Confirmed Line Array Helpers
// ==============================================================================================

// @function Deletes all lines in an array and clears the matching color array.
// @param lines Line array.
// @param colors Matching color array.
// @returns true.
export clearLines(array<line> lines, array<color> colors) =>
    if array.size(lines) > 0
        for i = array.size(lines) - 1 to 0
            line ln = array.get(lines, i)

            if not na(ln)
                line.delete(ln)

    array.clear(lines)
    array.clear(colors)

    true

// @function Pushes a confirmed oscillator-pane divergence line into line/color arrays.
// @param lines Line array.
// @param colors Matching line color array.
// @param show Whether this output is enabled.
// @param active Whether the divergence condition is active.
// @param x1 Start bar_index.
// @param y1 Start oscillator value.
// @param x2 End bar_index.
// @param y2 End oscillator value.
// @param lineColor Base line color.
// @param lineTransp Line transparency.
// @param lineWidth Line width.
// @param lineStyle User-facing line style string.
// @param maxLines Maximum confirmed lines to keep.
// @returns true.
export pushOscLine(
     array<line> lines,
     array<color> colors,
     bool show,
     bool active,
     int x1,
     float y1,
     int x2,
     float y2,
     color lineColor,
     int lineTransp,
     int lineWidth,
     simple string lineStyle,
     int maxLines) =>

    bool enabled =
         show and
         active and
         maxLines > 0 and
         not na(x1) and
         not na(y1) and
         not na(x2) and
         not na(y2) and
         not na(lineColor)

    color storedColor = color.new(lineColor, lineTransp)

    if enabled
        line newLine = line.new(x1=x1, y1=y1, x2=x2, y2=y2, xloc=xloc.bar_index, extend=extend.none, color=storedColor, style=divLineStyle(lineStyle), width=lineWidth)
        array.push(lines, newLine)
        array.push(colors, storedColor)

    while array.size(lines) > maxLines
        line oldLine = array.shift(lines)

        if array.size(colors) > 0
            array.shift(colors)

        if not na(oldLine)
            line.delete(oldLine)

    true

// @function Pushes a confirmed price-pane divergence line into line/color arrays.
// @param lines Line array.
// @param colors Matching line color array.
// @param show Whether this output is enabled.
// @param active Whether the divergence condition is active.
// @param x1 Start bar_index.
// @param y1 Start price value.
// @param x2 End bar_index.
// @param y2 End price value.
// @param lineColor Base line color.
// @param lineTransp Line transparency.
// @param lineWidth Line width.
// @param lineStyle User-facing line style string.
// @param maxLines Maximum confirmed lines to keep.
// @returns true.
export pushPriceLine(
     array<line> lines,
     array<color> colors,
     bool show,
     bool active,
     int x1,
     float y1,
     int x2,
     float y2,
     color lineColor,
     int lineTransp,
     int lineWidth,
     simple string lineStyle,
     int maxLines) =>

    bool enabled =
         show and
         active and
         maxLines > 0 and
         not na(x1) and
         not na(y1) and
         not na(x2) and
         not na(y2) and
         not na(lineColor)

    color storedColor = color.new(lineColor, lineTransp)

    if enabled
        line newLine = line.new(x1=x1, y1=y1, x2=x2, y2=y2, xloc=xloc.bar_index, extend=extend.none, color=storedColor, style=divLineStyle(lineStyle), width=lineWidth, force_overlay=true)
        array.push(lines, newLine)
        array.push(colors, storedColor)

    while array.size(lines) > maxLines
        line oldLine = array.shift(lines)

        if array.size(colors) > 0
            array.shift(colors)

        if not na(oldLine)
            line.delete(oldLine)

    true

// ==============================================================================================
// 🔴 END REGION: Confirmed Line Array Helpers
// ==============================================================================================


// ==============================================================================================
// 🟢 REGION: Confirmed Label Array Helpers
// ==============================================================================================

// @function Deletes all labels in an array and clears the matching color array.
// @param labels Label array.
// @param colors Matching color array.
// @returns true.
export clearLabels(array<label> labels, array<color> colors) =>
    while array.size(labels) > 0
        label oldLabel = array.pop(labels)

        if not na(oldLabel)
            label.delete(oldLabel)

    array.clear(colors)

    true

// @function Pushes a confirmed oscillator-pane divergence label into label/color arrays.
// @param labels Label array.
// @param colors Matching label color array.
// @param show Whether labels are enabled.
// @param active Whether the divergence condition is active.
// @param xIndex Label x bar_index.
// @param y Label y value.
// @param labelText Label text.
// @param styleText Style text: up, down, or none.
// @param lineColor Base label color.
// @param labelTextOnly If true, transparent background and colored text.
// @param labelBgTransp Label background transparency.
// @param labelSize Label size string.
// @param maxLabels Maximum confirmed labels to keep.
// @returns true.
export pushOscLabel(
     array<label> labels,
     array<color> colors,
     bool show,
     bool active,
     int xIndex,
     float y,
     string labelText,
     simple string styleText,
     color lineColor,
     bool labelTextOnly,
     int labelBgTransp,
     simple string labelSize,
     int maxLabels) =>

    bool enabled =
         show and
         active and
         maxLabels > 0 and
         not na(xIndex) and
         not na(y) and
         labelText != "" and
         not na(lineColor)

    if enabled
        string resolvedStyle =
             styleText == "down" ? label.style_label_down :
             styleText == "up" ? label.style_label_up : label.style_none

        color labelBg = labelTextOnly ? color.new(color.black, 100) : color.new(lineColor, labelBgTransp)
        color labelTxt = labelTextOnly ? color.new(lineColor, 0) : divContrastText(lineColor)

        label newLabel = label.new(x=xIndex, y=y, text=labelText, xloc=xloc.bar_index, yloc=yloc.price, style=resolvedStyle, color=labelBg, textcolor=labelTxt, size=divLabelSize(labelSize))
        array.push(labels, newLabel)
        array.push(colors, lineColor)

    while array.size(labels) > maxLabels
        label oldLabel = array.shift(labels)

        if array.size(colors) > 0
            array.shift(colors)

        if not na(oldLabel)
            label.delete(oldLabel)

    true

// @function Pushes a confirmed price-pane divergence label into label/color arrays.
// @param labels Label array.
// @param colors Matching label color array.
// @param show Whether labels are enabled.
// @param active Whether the divergence condition is active.
// @param xTime Label x time.
// @param labelText Label text.
// @param ylocText yloc text: above or below.
// @param styleText Style text: up, down, or none.
// @param lineColor Base label color.
// @param labelTextOnly If true, transparent background and colored text.
// @param labelBgTransp Label background transparency.
// @param labelSize Label size string.
// @param maxLabels Maximum confirmed labels to keep.
// @returns true.
export pushPriceLabel(
     array<label> labels,
     array<color> colors,
     bool show,
     bool active,
     int xTime,
     string labelText,
     simple string ylocText,
     simple string styleText,
     color lineColor,
     bool labelTextOnly,
     int labelBgTransp,
     simple string labelSize,
     int maxLabels) =>

    bool enabled =
         show and
         active and
         maxLabels > 0 and
         not na(xTime) and
         labelText != "" and
         not na(lineColor)

    if enabled
        string resolvedStyle =
             styleText == "down" ? label.style_label_down :
             styleText == "up" ? label.style_label_up : label.style_none

        string resolvedYloc =
             ylocText == "above" ? yloc.abovebar : yloc.belowbar

        color labelBg = labelTextOnly ? color.new(color.black, 100) : color.new(lineColor, labelBgTransp)
        color labelTxt = labelTextOnly ? color.new(lineColor, 0) : divContrastText(lineColor)

        label newLabel = label.new(x=xTime, y=0, text=labelText, xloc=xloc.bar_time, yloc=resolvedYloc, style=resolvedStyle, color=labelBg, textcolor=labelTxt, size=divLabelSize(labelSize), force_overlay=true)
        array.push(labels, newLabel)
        array.push(colors, lineColor)

    while array.size(labels) > maxLabels
        label oldLabel = array.shift(labels)

        if array.size(colors) > 0
            array.shift(colors)

        if not na(oldLabel)
            label.delete(oldLabel)

    true

// ==============================================================================================
// 🔴 END REGION: Confirmed Label Array Helpers
// ==============================================================================================

// ==============================================================================================
// 🟢 REGION: Indexed Last-N Object Helpers
// ==============================================================================================
//
// 📌 PURPOSE:
//     Adds Last-N-aware object lifecycle helpers for confirmed divergence/context outputs.
//
// 🧠 USER-FACING MODEL:
//     These helpers extend the original confirmed line/label helpers by storing a matching
//     bar_index for each object. This lets scripts prune old objects by Last N Bars while
//     also enforcing max-count budgets.
//
// Important design note:
//
// • Existing pushOscLine(), pushPriceLine(), pushOscLabel(), and pushPriceLabel()
//   remain unchanged for backward compatibility.
// • These indexed helpers are intended for newer scripts that want object pruning by
//   bar_index windows such as:
//      - Divergence Last N Bars
//      - Main Label Last N Bars
//      - Context Last N Bars
//      - Box Last N Bars
// • The calling script still decides the min index to keep:
//      int minIdxToKeep = math.max(last_bar_index - lastN + 1, 0)
//
// Array model:
//
// • lines  / labels = actual Pine objects
// • colors          = matching base/stored color
// • idxs            = matching bar_index used for Last-N pruning
//
// ==============================================================================================

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Indexed Clear Helpers
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// @function Deletes all indexed lines and clears matching color/index arrays.
// @param lines Line array.
// @param colors Matching color array.
// @param idxs Matching bar_index array.
// @returns true.
export clearIndexedLines(
     array<line> lines,
     array<color> colors,
     array<int> idxs) =>

    while array.size(lines) > 0
        line oldLine = array.pop(lines)

        if not na(oldLine)
            line.delete(oldLine)

    array.clear(colors)
    array.clear(idxs)

    true

// @function Deletes all indexed labels and clears matching color/index arrays.
// @param labels Label array.
// @param colors Matching color array.
// @param idxs Matching bar_index array.
// @returns true.
export clearIndexedLabels(
     array<label> labels,
     array<color> colors,
     array<int> idxs) =>

    while array.size(labels) > 0
        label oldLabel = array.pop(labels)

        if not na(oldLabel)
            label.delete(oldLabel)

    array.clear(colors)
    array.clear(idxs)

    true

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Indexed Prune Helpers
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// @function Prunes indexed lines by Last-N min index and max-count budget.
// @param lines Line array.
// @param colors Matching color array.
// @param idxs Matching bar_index array.
// @param maxLines Maximum lines to keep.
// @param minIdxToKeep Oldest allowed bar_index.
// @returns true.
export pruneIndexedLines(
     array<line> lines,
     array<color> colors,
     array<int> idxs,
     int maxLines,
     int minIdxToKeep) =>

    if maxLines <= 0
        clearIndexedLines(lines, colors, idxs)
    else
        int scanCount =
             math.min(array.size(lines), array.size(idxs))

        int i =
             scanCount - 1

        while i >= 0
            int objectIdx =
                 array.get(idxs, i)

            bool removeObject =
                 na(objectIdx) or objectIdx < minIdxToKeep

            if removeObject
                line oldLine =
                     array.get(lines, i)

                if not na(oldLine)
                    line.delete(oldLine)

                array.remove(lines, i)

                if i < array.size(colors)
                    array.remove(colors, i)

                array.remove(idxs, i)

            i -= 1

        while array.size(lines) > maxLines
            line oldLine =
                 array.shift(lines)

            if not na(oldLine)
                line.delete(oldLine)

            if array.size(colors) > 0
                array.shift(colors)

            if array.size(idxs) > 0
                array.shift(idxs)

    true

// @function Prunes indexed labels by Last-N min index and max-count budget.
// @param labels Label array.
// @param colors Matching color array.
// @param idxs Matching bar_index array.
// @param maxLabels Maximum labels to keep.
// @param minIdxToKeep Oldest allowed bar_index.
// @returns true.
export pruneIndexedLabels(
     array<label> labels,
     array<color> colors,
     array<int> idxs,
     int maxLabels,
     int minIdxToKeep) =>

    if maxLabels <= 0
        clearIndexedLabels(labels, colors, idxs)
    else
        int scanCount =
             math.min(array.size(labels), array.size(idxs))

        int i =
             scanCount - 1

        while i >= 0
            int objectIdx =
                 array.get(idxs, i)

            bool removeObject =
                 na(objectIdx) or objectIdx < minIdxToKeep

            if removeObject
                label oldLabel =
                     array.get(labels, i)

                if not na(oldLabel)
                    label.delete(oldLabel)

                array.remove(labels, i)

                if i < array.size(colors)
                    array.remove(colors, i)

                array.remove(idxs, i)

            i -= 1

        while array.size(labels) > maxLabels
            label oldLabel =
                 array.shift(labels)

            if not na(oldLabel)
                label.delete(oldLabel)

            if array.size(colors) > 0
                array.shift(colors)

            if array.size(idxs) > 0
                array.shift(idxs)

    true

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Indexed Confirmed Line Push Helpers
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// @function Pushes a confirmed oscillator-pane line with matching Last-N index.
// @param lines Line array.
// @param colors Matching line color array.
// @param idxs Matching bar_index array.
// @param show Whether this output is enabled.
// @param active Whether the condition is active.
// @param x1 Start bar_index.
// @param y1 Start oscillator value.
// @param x2 End bar_index.
// @param y2 End oscillator value.
// @param keepIdx Bar index used for Last-N pruning, usually x2.
// @param lineColor Base line color.
// @param lineTransp Line transparency.
// @param lineWidth Line width.
// @param lineStyle User-facing line style.
// @param maxLines Maximum lines to keep.
// @param minIdxToKeep Oldest allowed bar_index.
// @returns true.
export pushOscLineIndexed(
     array<line> lines,
     array<color> colors,
     array<int> idxs,
     bool show,
     bool active,
     int x1,
     float y1,
     int x2,
     float y2,
     int keepIdx,
     color lineColor,
     int lineTransp,
     int lineWidth,
     simple string lineStyle,
     int maxLines,
     int minIdxToKeep) =>

    bool enabled =
         show and
         active and
         maxLines > 0 and
         not na(x1) and
         not na(y1) and
         not na(x2) and
         not na(y2) and
         not na(lineColor)

    color storedColor =
         color.new(lineColor, lineTransp)

    int storedIdx =
         na(keepIdx) ? x2 : keepIdx

    if enabled
        line newLine =
             line.new(
                 x1=x1,
                 y1=y1,
                 x2=x2,
                 y2=y2,
                 xloc=xloc.bar_index,
                 extend=extend.none,
                 color=storedColor,
                 style=divLineStyle(lineStyle),
                 width=lineWidth)

        array.push(lines, newLine)
        array.push(colors, storedColor)
        array.push(idxs, storedIdx)

    pruneIndexedLines(lines, colors, idxs, maxLines, minIdxToKeep)

// @function Pushes a confirmed price-pane line with matching Last-N index.
// @param lines Line array.
// @param colors Matching line color array.
// @param idxs Matching bar_index array.
// @param show Whether this output is enabled.
// @param active Whether the condition is active.
// @param x1 Start bar_index.
// @param y1 Start price value.
// @param x2 End bar_index.
// @param y2 End price value.
// @param keepIdx Bar index used for Last-N pruning, usually x2.
// @param lineColor Base line color.
// @param lineTransp Line transparency.
// @param lineWidth Line width.
// @param lineStyle User-facing line style.
// @param maxLines Maximum lines to keep.
// @param minIdxToKeep Oldest allowed bar_index.
// @returns true.
export pushPriceLineIndexed(
     array<line> lines,
     array<color> colors,
     array<int> idxs,
     bool show,
     bool active,
     int x1,
     float y1,
     int x2,
     float y2,
     int keepIdx,
     color lineColor,
     int lineTransp,
     int lineWidth,
     simple string lineStyle,
     int maxLines,
     int minIdxToKeep) =>

    bool enabled =
         show and
         active and
         maxLines > 0 and
         not na(x1) and
         not na(y1) and
         not na(x2) and
         not na(y2) and
         not na(lineColor)

    color storedColor =
         color.new(lineColor, lineTransp)

    int storedIdx =
         na(keepIdx) ? x2 : keepIdx

    if enabled
        line newLine =
             line.new(
                 x1=x1,
                 y1=y1,
                 x2=x2,
                 y2=y2,
                 xloc=xloc.bar_index,
                 extend=extend.none,
                 color=storedColor,
                 style=divLineStyle(lineStyle),
                 width=lineWidth,
                 force_overlay=true)

        array.push(lines, newLine)
        array.push(colors, storedColor)
        array.push(idxs, storedIdx)

    pruneIndexedLines(lines, colors, idxs, maxLines, minIdxToKeep)

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Indexed Confirmed Label Push Helpers
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// @function Pushes a confirmed oscillator-pane label with matching Last-N index.
// @param labels Label array.
// @param colors Matching label color array.
// @param idxs Matching bar_index array.
// @param show Whether labels are enabled.
// @param active Whether the condition is active.
// @param xIndex Label x bar_index.
// @param y Label y value.
// @param keepIdx Bar index used for Last-N pruning, usually xIndex.
// @param labelText Label text.
// @param styleText Style text: up, down, or none.
// @param lineColor Base label color.
// @param labelTextOnly If true, transparent background and colored text.
// @param labelBgTransp Label background transparency.
// @param labelSize Label size string.
// @param maxLabels Maximum labels to keep.
// @param minIdxToKeep Oldest allowed bar_index.
// @returns true.
export pushOscLabelIndexed(
     array<label> labels,
     array<color> colors,
     array<int> idxs,
     bool show,
     bool active,
     int xIndex,
     float y,
     int keepIdx,
     string labelText,
     simple string styleText,
     color lineColor,
     bool labelTextOnly,
     int labelBgTransp,
     simple string labelSize,
     int maxLabels,
     int minIdxToKeep) =>

    bool enabled =
         show and
         active and
         maxLabels > 0 and
         not na(xIndex) and
         not na(y) and
         labelText != "" and
         not na(lineColor)

    int storedIdx =
         na(keepIdx) ? xIndex : keepIdx

    if enabled
        string resolvedStyle =
             styleText == "down" ? label.style_label_down :
             styleText == "up" ? label.style_label_up : label.style_none

        color labelBg =
             labelTextOnly ? color.new(color.black, 100) : color.new(lineColor, labelBgTransp)

        color labelTxt =
             labelTextOnly ? color.new(lineColor, 0) : divContrastText(lineColor)

        label newLabel =
             label.new(
                 x=xIndex,
                 y=y,
                 text=labelText,
                 xloc=xloc.bar_index,
                 yloc=yloc.price,
                 style=resolvedStyle,
                 color=labelBg,
                 textcolor=labelTxt,
                 size=divLabelSize(labelSize))

        array.push(labels, newLabel)
        array.push(colors, lineColor)
        array.push(idxs, storedIdx)

    pruneIndexedLabels(labels, colors, idxs, maxLabels, minIdxToKeep)

// @function Pushes a confirmed price-pane label with matching Last-N index.
// @param labels Label array.
// @param colors Matching label color array.
// @param idxs Matching bar_index array.
// @param show Whether labels are enabled.
// @param active Whether the condition is active.
// @param xTime Label x time.
// @param keepIdx Bar index used for Last-N pruning.
// @param labelText Label text.
// @param ylocText yloc text: above or below.
// @param styleText Style text: up, down, or none.
// @param lineColor Base label color.
// @param labelTextOnly If true, transparent background and colored text.
// @param labelBgTransp Label background transparency.
// @param labelSize Label size string.
// @param maxLabels Maximum labels to keep.
// @param minIdxToKeep Oldest allowed bar_index.
// @returns true.
export pushPriceLabelIndexed(
     array<label> labels,
     array<color> colors,
     array<int> idxs,
     bool show,
     bool active,
     int xTime,
     int keepIdx,
     string labelText,
     simple string ylocText,
     simple string styleText,
     color lineColor,
     bool labelTextOnly,
     int labelBgTransp,
     simple string labelSize,
     int maxLabels,
     int minIdxToKeep) =>

    bool enabled =
         show and
         active and
         maxLabels > 0 and
         not na(xTime) and
         not na(keepIdx) and
         labelText != "" and
         not na(lineColor)

    if enabled
        string resolvedStyle =
             styleText == "down" ? label.style_label_down :
             styleText == "up" ? label.style_label_up : label.style_none

        string resolvedYloc =
             ylocText == "above" ? yloc.abovebar : yloc.belowbar

        color labelBg =
             labelTextOnly ? color.new(color.black, 100) : color.new(lineColor, labelBgTransp)

        color labelTxt =
             labelTextOnly ? color.new(lineColor, 0) : divContrastText(lineColor)

        label newLabel =
             label.new(
                 x=xTime,
                 y=0,
                 text=labelText,
                 xloc=xloc.bar_time,
                 yloc=resolvedYloc,
                 style=resolvedStyle,
                 color=labelBg,
                 textcolor=labelTxt,
                 size=divLabelSize(labelSize),
                 force_overlay=true)

        array.push(labels, newLabel)
        array.push(colors, lineColor)
        array.push(idxs, keepIdx)

    pruneIndexedLabels(labels, colors, idxs, maxLabels, minIdxToKeep)

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Indexed Slot Visibility Helpers
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// @function Applies visible slot budget to indexed lines without deleting older objects.
// @param lines Line array.
// @param colors Matching color array.
// @param idxs Matching bar_index array.
// @param visibleSlots Number of most-recent eligible lines to keep visible.
// @param minIdxToKeep Oldest allowed bar_index.
// @returns true.
export applyIndexedLineSlots(
     array<line> lines,
     array<color> colors,
     array<int> idxs,
     int visibleSlots,
     int minIdxToKeep) =>

    int n =
         math.min(array.size(lines), array.size(idxs))

    int slots =
         math.max(visibleSlots, 0)

    int eligibleCount =
         0

    if n > 0
        for i = 0 to n - 1
            int objectIdx =
                 array.get(idxs, i)

            if not na(objectIdx) and objectIdx >= minIdxToKeep
                eligibleCount += 1

    int firstVisibleEligible =
         math.max(eligibleCount - slots, 0)

    int eligibleCursor =
         0

    if n > 0
        for i = 0 to n - 1
            line ln =
                 array.get(lines, i)

            int objectIdx =
                 array.get(idxs, i)

            bool eligible =
                 not na(objectIdx) and objectIdx >= minIdxToKeep

            bool visible =
                 eligible and slots > 0 and eligibleCursor >= firstVisibleEligible

            color baseColor =
                 i < array.size(colors) ? array.get(colors, i) : color.new(color.white, 0)

            if not na(ln)
                line.set_color(ln, visible ? baseColor : color.new(baseColor, 100))

            if eligible
                eligibleCursor += 1

    true

// @function Applies visible slot budget to indexed labels without deleting older objects.
// @param labels Label array.
// @param colors Matching color array.
// @param idxs Matching bar_index array.
// @param visibleSlots Number of most-recent eligible labels to keep visible.
// @param minIdxToKeep Oldest allowed bar_index.
// @param labelTextOnly If true, transparent background and colored text.
// @param labelBgTransp Label background transparency.
// @returns true.
export applyIndexedLabelSlots(
     array<label> labels,
     array<color> colors,
     array<int> idxs,
     int visibleSlots,
     int minIdxToKeep,
     bool labelTextOnly,
     int labelBgTransp) =>

    int n =
         math.min(array.size(labels), array.size(idxs))

    int slots =
         math.max(visibleSlots, 0)

    int eligibleCount =
         0

    if n > 0
        for i = 0 to n - 1
            int objectIdx =
                 array.get(idxs, i)

            if not na(objectIdx) and objectIdx >= minIdxToKeep
                eligibleCount += 1

    int firstVisibleEligible =
         math.max(eligibleCount - slots, 0)

    int eligibleCursor =
         0

    if n > 0
        for i = 0 to n - 1
            label lbl =
                 array.get(labels, i)

            int objectIdx =
                 array.get(idxs, i)

            bool eligible =
                 not na(objectIdx) and objectIdx >= minIdxToKeep

            bool visible =
                 eligible and slots > 0 and eligibleCursor >= firstVisibleEligible

            color baseColor =
                 i < array.size(colors) ? array.get(colors, i) : color.new(color.white, 0)

            if not na(lbl)
                color labelBg =
                     visible
                     ? labelTextOnly ? color.new(color.black, 100) : color.new(baseColor, labelBgTransp)
                     : color.new(color.black, 100)

                color labelTxt =
                     visible
                     ? labelTextOnly ? color.new(baseColor, 0) : divContrastText(baseColor)
                     : color.new(baseColor, 100)

                label.set_color(lbl, labelBg)
                label.set_textcolor(lbl, labelTxt)

            if eligible
                eligibleCursor += 1

    true


// ==============================================================================================
// 🔴 END REGION: Indexed Last-N Object Helpers
// ==============================================================================================

// ==============================================================================================
// 🟢 REGION: Confirmed Slot Visibility Helpers
// ==============================================================================================

// @function Applies visible slot budget to confirmed line arrays without deleting older objects.
// @param lines Line array.
// @param colors Matching color array.
// @param visibleSlots Number of most-recent confirmed lines to keep visible.
// @returns true.
export applyLineSlots(array<line> lines, array<color> colors, int visibleSlots) =>
    int n = array.size(lines)
    int slots = math.max(visibleSlots, 0)
    int firstVisible = math.max(n - slots, 0)

    if n > 0
        for i = 0 to n - 1
            line ln = array.get(lines, i)

            if not na(ln)
                color baseColor = i < array.size(colors) ? array.get(colors, i) : color.new(color.white, 0)
                color finalColor = i >= firstVisible and slots > 0 ? baseColor : color.new(baseColor, 100)
                line.set_color(ln, finalColor)

    true

// @function Applies visible slot budget to confirmed label arrays without deleting older objects.
// @param labels Label array.
// @param colors Matching label color array.
// @param visibleSlots Number of most-recent confirmed labels to keep visible.
// @param labelTextOnly If true, transparent background and colored text.
// @param labelBgTransp Label background transparency.
// @returns true.
export applyLabelSlots(
     array<label> labels,
     array<color> colors,
     int visibleSlots,
     bool labelTextOnly,
     int labelBgTransp) =>

    int n = array.size(labels)
    int slots = math.max(visibleSlots, 0)
    int firstVisible = math.max(n - slots, 0)

    if n > 0
        for i = 0 to n - 1
            label lbl = array.get(labels, i)

            if not na(lbl)
                color baseColor = i < array.size(colors) ? array.get(colors, i) : color.new(color.white, 0)
                bool visible = i >= firstVisible and slots > 0

                color labelBg = visible ? (labelTextOnly ? color.new(color.black, 100) : color.new(baseColor, labelBgTransp)) : color.new(color.black, 100)
                color labelTxt = visible ? (labelTextOnly ? color.new(baseColor, 0) : divContrastText(baseColor)) : color.new(baseColor, 100)

                label.set_color(lbl, labelBg)
                label.set_textcolor(lbl, labelTxt)

    true

// ==============================================================================================
// 🔴 END REGION: Confirmed Slot Visibility Helpers
// ==============================================================================================


// ==============================================================================================
// 🟢 REGION: Live Preview Line Helpers
// ==============================================================================================

// @function Creates, updates, or deletes a live oscillator-pane divergence line.
// @param ln Existing line.
// @param show Whether live line should exist.
// @param x1 Start bar_index.
// @param y1 Start value.
// @param x2 End bar_index.
// @param y2 End value.
// @param lineColor Line color.
// @param lineWidth Line width.
// @param lineStyle Line style string.
// @returns Updated line.
export syncLiveOscLine(
     line ln,
     bool show,
     int x1,
     float y1,
     int x2,
     float y2,
     color lineColor,
     int lineWidth,
     simple string lineStyle) =>

    line out = ln

    if show and not na(x1) and not na(y1) and not na(x2) and not na(y2)
        if na(out)
            out := line.new(x1=x1, y1=y1, x2=x2, y2=y2, xloc=xloc.bar_index, extend=extend.none, color=lineColor, width=lineWidth, style=divLineStyle(lineStyle))
        else
            line.set_xy1(out, x1, y1)
            line.set_xy2(out, x2, y2)
            line.set_color(out, lineColor)
            line.set_width(out, lineWidth)
            line.set_style(out, divLineStyle(lineStyle))
    else
        if not na(out)
            line.delete(out)
            out := na

    out

// @function Creates, updates, or deletes a live price-pane divergence line.
// @param ln Existing line.
// @param show Whether live line should exist.
// @param x1 Start bar_index.
// @param y1 Start price.
// @param x2 End bar_index.
// @param y2 End price.
// @param lineColor Line color.
// @param lineWidth Line width.
// @param lineStyle Line style string.
// @returns Updated line.
export syncLivePriceLine(
     line ln,
     bool show,
     int x1,
     float y1,
     int x2,
     float y2,
     color lineColor,
     int lineWidth,
     simple string lineStyle) =>

    line out = ln

    if show and not na(x1) and not na(y1) and not na(x2) and not na(y2)
        if na(out)
            out := line.new(x1=x1, y1=y1, x2=x2, y2=y2, xloc=xloc.bar_index, extend=extend.none, color=lineColor, width=lineWidth, style=divLineStyle(lineStyle), force_overlay=true)
        else
            line.set_xy1(out, x1, y1)
            line.set_xy2(out, x2, y2)
            line.set_color(out, lineColor)
            line.set_width(out, lineWidth)
            line.set_style(out, divLineStyle(lineStyle))
    else
        if not na(out)
            line.delete(out)
            out := na

    out

// ==============================================================================================
// 🔴 END REGION: Live Preview Line Helpers
// ==============================================================================================


